WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:05.188
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B two, Book three.

2
00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:09.396
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:09.696 --> 00:00:15.890
Unit thirteen: Global Citizenship. Today you will use abstract subjects with the passive.

4
00:00:16.190 --> 00:00:18.912
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:19.867 --> 00:00:23.541
Part one: words. You will learn twelve new words.

6
00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:25.849
Interconnected world.

7
00:00:26.850 --> 00:00:29.871
Interconnected world means a world where everything is linked.

8
00:00:30.483 --> 00:00:32.599
We live in an interconnected world.

9
00:00:33.183 --> 00:00:36.532
Your turn. Say: Interconnected world.

10
00:00:39.367 --> 00:00:40.890
Interconnected world.

11
00:00:41.650 --> 00:00:43.417
Global responsibility.

12
00:00:44.417 --> 00:00:48.030
Global responsibility means a duty we all share for the planet.

13
00:00:48.617 --> 00:00:51.615
Fighting poverty is a global responsibility.

14
00:00:52.217 --> 00:00:55.798
Your turn. Say: Global responsibility.

15
00:00:58.633 --> 00:01:00.656
Global responsibility.

16
00:01:01.417 --> 00:01:02.905
Cultural diplomacy.

17
00:01:03.917 --> 00:01:08.447
Cultural diplomacy means using culture to build friendship between countries.

18
00:01:09.050 --> 00:01:11.735
Dance tours are a form of cultural diplomacy.

19
00:01:12.350 --> 00:01:15.711
Your turn. Say: Cultural diplomacy.

20
00:01:18.567 --> 00:01:20.241
Cultural diplomacy.

21
00:01:20.983 --> 00:01:22.495
Transnational issue.

22
00:01:23.483 --> 00:01:26.864
Transnational issue means a problem that crosses borders.

23
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.786
Pollution is a transnational issue.

24
00:01:30.383 --> 00:01:33.709
Your turn. Say: Transnational issue.

25
00:01:36.567 --> 00:01:38.578
Transnational issue.

26
00:01:39.317 --> 00:01:40.724
Universal value.

27
00:01:41.717 --> 00:01:44.866
Universal value means a belief shared by all people.

28
00:01:45.450 --> 00:01:47.542
Kindness is a universal value.

29
00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:51.522
Your turn. Say: Universal value.

30
00:01:54.367 --> 00:01:55.913
Universal value.

31
00:01:56.650 --> 00:01:58.545
Cosmopolitan mindset.

32
00:01:59.550 --> 00:02:03.070
Cosmopolitan mindset means feeling at home with many cultures.

33
00:02:03.683 --> 00:02:06.182
Travel gave her a cosmopolitan mindset.

34
00:02:06.783 --> 00:02:10.353
Your turn. Say: Cosmopolitan mindset.

35
00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:15.060
Cosmopolitan mindset.

36
00:02:15.817 --> 00:02:17.317
Global solidarity.

37
00:02:18.317 --> 00:02:21.918
Global solidarity means standing together across the world.

38
00:02:22.517 --> 00:02:25.236
Global solidarity helped after the earthquake.

39
00:02:25.850 --> 00:02:28.955
Your turn. Say: Global solidarity.

40
00:02:31.800 --> 00:02:33.533
Global solidarity.

41
00:02:34.283 --> 00:02:35.551
Shared humanity.

42
00:02:36.550 --> 00:02:39.861
Shared humanity means what all people have in common.

43
00:02:40.450 --> 00:02:42.972
Music reminds us of our shared humanity.

44
00:02:43.583 --> 00:02:46.874
Your turn. Say: Shared humanity.

45
00:02:49.733 --> 00:02:50.967
Shared humanity.

46
00:02:51.717 --> 00:02:53.809
Cross-border collaboration.

47
00:02:54.817 --> 00:02:58.326
Cross-border collaboration means countries working together.

48
00:02:58.917 --> 00:03:01.845
Cross-border collaboration protects the Mekong.

49
00:03:02.450 --> 00:03:07.227
Your turn. Say: Cross-border collaboration.

50
00:03:10.067 --> 00:03:12.925
Cross-border collaboration.

51
00:03:13.683 --> 00:03:15.068
World awareness.

52
00:03:16.083 --> 00:03:19.070
World awareness means knowing about the wider world.

53
00:03:19.683 --> 00:03:21.962
Reading news builds world awareness.

54
00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:25.446
Your turn. Say: World awareness.

55
00:03:28.300 --> 00:03:29.719
World awareness.

56
00:03:30.483 --> 00:03:31.926
Ethical globalism.

57
00:03:32.917 --> 00:03:36.623
Ethical globalism means global connection based on fairness.

58
00:03:37.217 --> 00:03:39.553
Ethical globalism means fair trade.

59
00:03:40.150 --> 00:03:43.441
Your turn. Say: Ethical globalism.

60
00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:47.963
Ethical globalism.

61
00:03:48.717 --> 00:03:49.996
Collective future.

62
00:03:50.983 --> 00:03:53.540
Collective future means the future we share.

63
00:03:54.150 --> 00:03:56.788
Our collective future depends on cooperation.

64
00:03:57.383 --> 00:04:00.221
Your turn. Say: Collective future.

65
00:04:03.067 --> 00:04:04.370
Collective future.

66
00:04:05.167 --> 00:04:09.061
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

67
00:04:09.917 --> 00:04:12.613
Visal, how can we solve problems like pollution?

68
00:04:13.717 --> 00:04:19.048
Global issues are best addressed through cross-border collaboration.

69
00:04:20.150 --> 00:04:21.848
Why not one country alone?

70
00:04:22.950 --> 00:04:28.052
Because the Mekong is shared by six countries. It must be protected together.

71
00:04:29.150 --> 00:04:30.302
What is your role?

72
00:04:31.417 --> 00:04:36.504
Universal values should be taught in every school, so we all feel connected.

73
00:04:37.667 --> 00:04:39.190
Part three: grammar.

74
00:04:40.050 --> 00:04:43.710
Grammar focus: Abstract subject plus passive.

75
00:04:44.010 --> 00:04:45.220
Look at the pattern.

76
00:04:45.917 --> 00:04:49.716
Global issues are best addressed through cross-border collaboration.

77
00:04:50.617 --> 00:04:53.615
Universal values should be taught in every school.

78
00:04:54.517 --> 00:04:57.712
Our collective future is shaped by today's choices.

79
00:04:58.667 --> 00:05:05.275
With abstract subjects like 'issues' or 'values', the passive sounds formal and focuses on the idea, not the person.

80
00:05:06.017 --> 00:05:10.550
Be careful! Don't say: Global issues are best address together.

81
00:05:12.500 --> 00:05:16.020
Say: Global issues are best addressed together.

82
00:05:16.320 --> 00:05:18.633
The passive needs the past participle.

83
00:05:19.433 --> 00:05:21.842
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

84
00:05:22.633 --> 00:05:23.658
One World.

85
00:05:23.958 --> 00:05:26.027
We live in an interconnected world.

86
00:05:27.033 --> 00:05:30.461
Transnational issues cannot be solved by one country alone.

87
00:05:31.467 --> 00:05:35.928
Global issues are best addressed through cross-border collaboration.

88
00:05:36.933 --> 00:05:40.558
Global solidarity and shared humanity unite us.

89
00:05:41.567 --> 00:05:44.762
Our collective future is built on universal values.

90
00:05:45.867 --> 00:05:50.043
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

91
00:05:50.883 --> 00:05:53.080
Global issues are best blank together.

92
00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:57.173
A, addressed. B, address. C, addressing.

93
00:06:00.733 --> 00:06:02.570
The answer is A: addressed.

94
00:06:03.717 --> 00:06:06.517
A problem that crosses borders is a blank issue.

95
00:06:06.817 --> 00:06:11.272
A, transnational. B, universal. C, cultural.

96
00:06:14.833 --> 00:06:17.379
The answer is A: transnational.

97
00:06:18.517 --> 00:06:21.248
What all people have in common is our shared blank.

98
00:06:21.548 --> 00:06:25.526
A, humanity. B, future. C, value.

99
00:06:29.067 --> 00:06:31.113
The answer is A: humanity.

100
00:06:32.300 --> 00:06:35.405
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

101
00:06:36.250 --> 00:06:38.691
What does being a 'global citizen' mean to you?

102
00:06:47.483 --> 00:06:49.065
Now listen to Visal.

103
00:06:49.365 --> 00:07:00.678
To me, a global citizen cares about people everywhere. Problems like climate change are best solved together, so I try to learn about other countries.

104
00:07:00.978 --> 00:07:02.653
Excellent answer, Visal!

105
00:07:03.550 --> 00:07:08.652
Great work! Now you can use twelve new words and abstract subject plus passive.

106
00:07:08.952 --> 00:07:14.742
Today's value is global citizenship. We all share one world. Help people near and far.

107
00:07:15.042 --> 00:07:17.764
See you in Unit fourteen. Goodbye!

108
00:07:18.064 --> 00:07:21.552
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

